    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a per-city capacity rule to `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the existing OfficeFloor endpoint conventions (function-per-step, checked-exception + escalation handler), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitively, matching the counting already used by `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`) via `ownerRepository.findAll()`, and throws `OwnerCityFullException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n\n2. **`OwnerCityFullException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces on the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`OwnerCityFullExceptionHandler`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with an `OwnerValidationErrors([\"city\"])` body, mirroring the existing duplicate-household 409 handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026OwnerCityFullException.yml` mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` between the `household` check and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps, so the count reflects existing owners before the new one is saved.\n\nThe new step runs before the owner is built/saved, so the 50 existing owners are counted and the 51st create is rejected. Test results: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` passes and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
